pragma silverscript ^0.1.0;

// KpfPendingO: a part of an oracle-market pair (KpfPairO) against which a price claim vouched by the pair's underwriter
// is pending (docs/DESIGN-ORACLE-2.md 1.5, 1.7; what is built and every deviation: docs/DESIGN-ORACLE-IMPL.md, third
// slice). KpfPairO.propose writes it under a fresh covenant id that it checks (no input and no other output carries
// it), so the id names this claim alone: its dispute, receipts and pool, and the restored, cured or forfeited part,
// continue that id; only the status window (status, P, disputer) ever changes.
// DESIGN: review 6 (R6-F1, R6-F2): KpfPending lives under its pair's id (one id, two templates); here a claim's id is
// unique to it, so a dispute or pool of one claim can never be taken for another's, whatever the DAA scores.
// DESIGN: review 7 (R7-F1): the fresh id proves the part new, not whose it is; the part also names the outpoint of the
// pair input that proposed it (mkParent), so no second pair can propose into it.
//
// Statuses: 1 pending, 2 contested, 3 upheld, 4 refuted.
//   pending    contest(u, dOut)  anyone with aged judge stake (KpfStake.open on NO in the same transaction): the part
//                                becomes contested, recording P (this UTXO's DAA score, exact) and the opener's key
//              cure(s)           kind 2 only, the loser's signature: the loser's bound moves to cureBound, the proposer
//                                (the underwriter) is repaid its refund
//              finalize()        anyone, once challengeDaa old (CSV): settle, or restore when the claim is void
//   contested  decide(d)         anyone, in the transaction that resolves the dispute (KpfStake.resolve naming this
//                                input): upheld if YES leads, refuted if NO leads, upheld whatever the verdict when the
//                                contest was accepted after the window (P + challengeDaa or later)
//   upheld     finalize()        anyone, at once: settle, or restore when the claim is void
//   refuted    finalize()        anyone, at once: restore; the bond goes to the defender, the disputer's share to it
//
// The claim is valid (it may settle) only if P + challengeDaa <= expiry (its whole window lies inside the cover),
// expiry <= P + termDaa + stepDaa (the bound of slice A: a pair a genesis made can rely on a slot it never bound for at
// most one period), and P - t0 <= lateDaa (a vouched claim landed later than the market allows is void). P is this
// UTXO's own DAA score while pending, the recorded one once contested.
// DESIGN: the note (1.5) judges a late claim at tau = P instead of voiding it, and lets a claim be accepted up to the
// expiry X; here a late claim is void and a claim must land at least challengeDaa before X, so no claim is ever pending
// beyond its cover and an honest underwriter is never judged at a price it did not sign.
// DESIGN: the note's live dispute has no deadline the covenant can enforce (time has only lower bounds); here the
// deadline is enforced after the fact: the contested part's own DAA score (the contest's acceptance, exact when decide
// reads it) must be below P + challengeDaa, or the verdict is ignored and the claim settles as if uncontested. A timely
// contest and a finalize (age >= challengeDaa) can therefore never both be valid.
//
// Bond, refund and fee (DESIGN 4.5d, the slash of DESIGN-ORACLE-2.md 1.7):
//   - the bond B (max(bondMin, 0.02 KAS, q(n, coverRate * sigmaBps / 10^4))) is in this part, posted by the claim's
//     proposer: the underwriter for a liquidation (kind 2), the closer for a close (kind 1, which the closer signs and
//     the underwriter co-signs); refund = B, plus the carrier the proposer funded when n < s;
//   - uncontested or upheld and valid: the proposer gets its refund (a liquidation: B + fee to the underwriter);
//   - refuted: the part is restored (value >= v - B), the disputer (the opening staker) gets floor(B * betaBps / 10^4) at
//     output M - 1 - i, the defender (the party the claim would have wronged) the rest at output i;
//   - void (and not refuted): the part is restored, the defender gets B: a claim that cannot settle costs its proposer
//     its bond, so a proposer cannot freeze a pair with void claims for free.
// DESIGN: the note has no proposer bond ("the slot is liable") and no rule for a void claim; here every claim carries a
// bond, a close's is posted by the closer (who signs the claim; the underwriter co-signs the price), and a void claim's
// bond goes to the defender.
// DESIGN: closed markets (the note's 4): the covenant cannot read a calendar (DAA is not wall time, time has only lower
// bounds). It enforces t0 <= tx.daa at the proposal and P - t0 <= lateDaa here, so no claim prices the future and none
// lands long after the moment it prices; whether t0 lies in a closed session is the feed definition's, and a claim
// about a closed session is false by definition: the judge refutes it when contested.
// DESIGN: the note slashes sigma x c from the underwriter's slot by a reservation at the opening of the dispute (1.7).
// A reservation needs the slot to authenticate the contested claim, which it cannot: a genesis can create a look-alike
// pending part naming any slot, so a reservation entry that accepts it lets anyone slash honest slots, and pinning this
// template in KpfBond would not help (a look-alike passes the template check). So the slash is posted with the claim
// itself, by the proposer's own funds, exactly as the book market's proposer bond; the slot only caps the cover (rho)
// and is never slashed in this slice.
//
// Every branch ends in a KpfPairO state precomputed by propose (restore, cure, forfeit; P2SH hashes, tags 0, unlisted) or
// in plain outputs; contest hands the part to the judge, whose resolution (anyone, after its round) delivers the
// verdict here; finalize needs no key and no evidence. So no part is locked: a pending part is finalized by anyone after
// challengeDaa, a contested one is decided when its dispute resolves (KpfStake.resolve, anyone), a decided one at once.
contract KpfPendingO(
    byte[32] JUDGE_TPL,
    int JUDGE_PRE,
    int JUDGE_SUF,
    byte[4] OPEN_TAG,
    byte[4] RESOLVE_TAG,
    byte[32] init_market,
    int init_rhoBps,
    int init_stepDaa,
    int init_termDaa,
    int init_tailDaa,
    int init_rateDaa,
    int init_slotUnbondDaa,
    int init_muBps,
    int init_ageDaa,
    int init_unbondDaa,
    int init_roundDaa,
    int init_burnBps,
    int init_minStake,
    byte[32] init_feedHash,
    int init_scale,
    int init_priceMax,
    int init_mmrBps,
    int init_gBps,
    int init_liqFeeBps,
    int init_keeperFeeMin,
    int init_minSize,
    int init_carrier,
    int init_idleDaa,
    int init_challengeDaa,
    int init_lateDaa,
    int init_quietDaa,
    int init_sigmaBps,
    int init_betaBps,
    int init_bondMin,
    int init_kind,
    int init_side,
    int init_n,
    int init_bl,
    int init_bs,
    int init_quote,
    int init_t0,
    int init_cureBound,
    int init_fee,
    int init_bond,
    int init_refund,
    int init_status,
    int init_clock,
    pubkey init_disputerKey,
    int init_entryPrice,
    pubkey init_longKey,
    pubkey init_shortKey,
    byte[32] init_uwId,
    pubkey init_uwKey,
    int init_coverRate,
    int init_expiry,
    int init_premium,
    int init_longAsk,
    int init_longMin,
    int init_longTip,
    int init_shortBid,
    int init_shortMin,
    int init_shortTip,
    byte[32] init_restoreHash,
    byte[32] init_cureHash,
    byte[32] init_forfeitHash,
    byte[32] init_mkParent
) {
    // The oracle market block (state [0..309)), byte for byte the pair's (KpfPairO describes every field).
    byte[32] market = init_market;
    int rhoBps = init_rhoBps;
    int stepDaa = init_stepDaa;
    int termDaa = init_termDaa;
    int tailDaa = init_tailDaa;
    int rateDaa = init_rateDaa;
    int slotUnbondDaa = init_slotUnbondDaa;
    int muBps = init_muBps;
    int ageDaa = init_ageDaa;
    int unbondDaa = init_unbondDaa;
    int roundDaa = init_roundDaa;
    int burnBps = init_burnBps;
    int minStake = init_minStake;
    byte[32] feedHash = init_feedHash;
    int scale = init_scale;
    int priceMax = init_priceMax;
    int mmrBps = init_mmrBps;
    int gBps = init_gBps;
    int liqFeeBps = init_liqFeeBps;
    int keeperFeeMin = init_keeperFeeMin;
    int minSize = init_minSize;
    int carrier = init_carrier;
    int idleDaa = init_idleDaa;
    int challengeDaa = init_challengeDaa;
    int lateDaa = init_lateDaa;
    int quietDaa = init_quietDaa;
    int sigmaBps = init_sigmaBps;
    int betaBps = init_betaBps;
    int bondMin = init_bondMin;
    // The claim (state [309..408)).
    int kind = init_kind;                // 1 close, 2 liquidation
    int side = init_side;                // kind 1: the closer; kind 2: the loser
    int n = init_n;
    int bl = init_bl;
    int bs = init_bs;
    int quote = init_quote;              // p, the price the underwriter vouched (sompi per whole unit)
    int t0 = init_t0;                    // the DAA the price refers to (the proposal's lock time proved tx.daa >= t0)
    int cureBound = init_cureBound;      // kind 2: the loser's bound after a cure (0: no cure)
    int fee = init_fee;                  // kind 2: keeper fee, to the underwriter at settlement
    int bond = init_bond;                // B
    int refund = init_refund;            // B, plus the carrier the proposer funded when n < s
    // The status window (state [408..459)): the only bytes contest and decide change.
    int status = init_status;            // 1 pending, 2 contested, 3 upheld, 4 refuted
    int clock = init_clock;              // P once contested (0 while pending)
    pubkey disputerKey = init_disputerKey; // the opening staker once contested (zero while pending)
    // The pair's entry, keys, binding and listings when the claim was proposed (state [459..681)), then the pair states
    // this part may become (state [681..780)).
    int entryPrice = init_entryPrice;
    pubkey longKey = init_longKey;
    pubkey shortKey = init_shortKey;
    byte[32] uwId = init_uwId;
    pubkey uwKey = init_uwKey;
    int coverRate = init_coverRate;
    int expiry = init_expiry;
    int premium = init_premium;
    int longAsk = init_longAsk;
    int longMin = init_longMin;
    int longTip = init_longTip;
    int shortBid = init_shortBid;
    int shortMin = init_shortMin;
    int shortTip = init_shortTip;
    byte[32] restoreHash = init_restoreHash;
    byte[32] cureHash = init_cureHash;
    byte[32] forfeitHash = init_forfeitHash;
    // The maker (review 7, R7-F1; state [780..813)): the outpoint commitment of the pair input whose propose wrote this
    // part (KpfPairO.me), so two pairs that would write one pending state never both accept one output. It lives for one
    // transaction: contest and decide write it zero, and no state this part becomes carries it.
    byte[32] mkParent = init_mkParent;

    byte constant SIGHASH_ALL = 0x01;
    int constant SIDE_LONG = 1;
    int constant SIDE_SHORT = 2;
    int constant KIND_CLOSE = 1;
    int constant PENDING = 1;
    int constant CONTESTED = 2;
    int constant UPHELD = 3;
    int constant REFUTED = 4;
    int constant YES = 1;
    int constant BPS = 10000;
    int constant PLAIN_DUST = 2000000;
    int constant RING = 12;
    int constant CSV_LIMIT = 4294967296;
    int constant RHO_MAX_BPS = 50000;
    int constant MU_MIN_BPS = 11000;
    int constant MU_MAX_BPS = 15000;
    int constant BURN_MAX_BPS = 5000;
    int constant MIN_STAKE_MAX = 1000000000000;
    int constant ROUND_MAX = 2592000;
    int constant AGE_MAX = 25920000;
    int constant UNBOND_MAX = 77760000;
    int constant UNIT = 1000000000;
    int constant SCALE_MAX = 1000000000;
    int constant PRICE_CAP = 100000000000000;
    int constant MMR_CAP = 5000;
    int constant BOND_MIN_MAX = 1000000000000;
    // Redeem offsets (the state starts at byte 1): the market body hashed into the id [34..310); the status window
    // [409..460); the maker push [781..814); the end of the state 814.
    int constant BODY_AT = 34;
    int constant BLOCK_END = 310;
    int constant STATUS_AT = 409;
    int constant DISPUTER_END = 460;
    int constant MAKER_AT = 781;
    int constant STATE_END = 814;
    // The judge block of the market: the id push [1..34) and the six judge parameters [88..142).
    int constant JUDGE_AT = 88;
    int constant JUDGE_END = 142;
    // KpfStake: its state length, the statuses read here, and the offsets within its state (redeem offset - 1).
    int constant STAKE_STATE_LEN = 270;
    int constant STAKE_FREE = 4;
    int constant STAKE_DISPUTE = 7;
    int constant STAKE_STATUS_AT = 33;
    int constant STAKE_MARKET_AT = 42;
    int constant STAKE_MARKET_END = 129;
    int constant STAKE_SIDE_AT = 162;
    // KpfStake.open's signature script: three 8-byte pushes, the 65-byte signature, the 4-byte dispatch tag, then the
    // redeem script (OP_PUSHDATA2, 3 bytes of header). KpfStake.resolve's: one 8-byte push, the tag, the redeem script.
    int constant OPEN_SIG_AT = 27;
    int constant OPEN_TAG_AT = 93;
    int constant OPEN_HEAD = 101;
    int constant RESOLVE_TAG_AT = 9;
    int constant RESOLVE_HEAD = 17;

    // As KpfPair.quoteOf.
    function quoteOf(int x, int r, int c) : int {
        int m = x % scale;
        int q = x / scale;
        return q * r + m * (r / scale) + (m * (r % scale) + c) / scale;
    }

    function signedBy(sig s, pubkey k) {
        byte[] sb = byte[](s);
        require(sb.length == 65);
        require(sb[64] == SIGHASH_ALL);
        require(checkSig(s, k));
    }

    function payTo(int j, pubkey k, int v) {
        if (v > 0) {
            require(tx.outputs[j].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2PK(k)));
            require(tx.outputs[j].value >= v);
        }
    }

    function clampP(int p) : int {
        int c = p;
        if (c < bl) { c = bl; }
        if (c > bs) { c = bs; }
        return c;
    }

    function ownRs() : byte[] {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        int len = OpTxInputScriptSigLen(self);
        return OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(self, len - this.bytecodeSize, len);
    }

    function i9(int c) : byte[] {
        return byte[](0x08) + byte[](c as byte[8]);
    }

    // The single output of this id: the P2SH of the hash h, holding at least v.
    function only(byte[32] h, int v) {
        byte[32] selfId = OpInputCovenantId(this.activeInputIndex);
        require(OpCovOutputCount(selfId) == 1);
        int o = OpCovOutputIdx(selfId, 0);
        require(tx.outputs[o].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2SH(h)));
        require(tx.outputs[o].value >= v);
    }

    // This part's continuation at output `self` with the status window w (51 bytes) and the maker zero, and the guards
    // of an entry that continues it (contest, decide).
    function cont(byte[] w) {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        byte[] rs = ownRs();
        byte[] z8 = byte[](0 as byte[8]);
        require(tx.outputs[self].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2SHFromRedeemScript(rs.slice(0, STATUS_AT) + w
            + rs.slice(DISPUTER_END, MAKER_AT) + byte[](0x20) + z8 + z8 + z8 + z8 + rs.slice(STATE_END, this.bytecodeSize))));
        require(OpOutputCovenantId(self) == OpInputCovenantId(self));
        require(tx.outputs[self].value >= tx.inputs[self].value);
    }

    // As KpfPair.tplState.
    function tplState(int idx, int pre, int stLen, int suf, byte[32] tpl) : byte[] {
        int sz = pre + stLen + suf;
        int base = OpTxInputScriptSigLen(idx) - sz;
        byte[] rs = OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(idx, base, base + sz);
        require(tx.inputs[idx].scriptPubKey == byte[](new ScriptPubKeyP2SHFromRedeemScript(rs)));
        require(blake3(byte[](pre as byte[8]) + rs.slice(0, pre) + byte[](suf as byte[8]) + rs.slice(pre + stLen, sz)) == tpl);
        return rs.slice(pre, pre + stLen);
    }

    // The 8-byte push at offset `at` of input u's signature script.
    function push8(int u, int at) : int {
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(u, at, at + 1) == byte[](0x08));
        return int(byte[8](OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(u, at + 1, at + 9)));
    }

    // As KpfClaimStub.canon: a KpfStake state whose every field is a canonical push.
    function canon(byte[] st) {
        require(st.length == STAKE_STATE_LEN);
        require(st.slice(0, 1) == byte[](0x20));
        require(st.slice(33, 34) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(42, 43) == byte[](0x20));
        require(st.slice(75, 76) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(84, 85) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(93, 94) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(102, 103) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(111, 112) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(120, 121) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(129, 130) == byte[](0x20));
        require(st.slice(162, 163) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(171, 172) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(180, 181) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(189, 190) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(198, 199) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(207, 208) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(216, 217) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(225, 226) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(234, 235) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(243, 244) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(252, 253) == byte[](0x08));
        require(st.slice(261, 262) == byte[](0x08));
    }

    // The judge block of this market (87 bytes): what a KpfStake of this market carries at its state [42..129).
    function judgeBlock(byte[] rs) : byte[] {
        return rs.slice(1, BODY_AT) + rs.slice(JUDGE_AT, JUDGE_END);
    }

    // The bond bounds of KpfBond.checkBond, the same text with the slot's unbonding delay named slotUnbondDaa
    // (`oracle_attack_tests` enforces it).
    // BEGIN oracle bond bounds
    function checkBond() {
        require(rhoBps >= BPS);
        require(rhoBps <= RHO_MAX_BPS);
        require(stepDaa > 0);
        require(termDaa >= stepDaa);
        require(termDaa % stepDaa == 0);
        require(termDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
        require(tailDaa >= 0);
        require(tailDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
        require(termDaa + tailDaa + 2 * stepDaa <= RING * stepDaa);
        require(rateDaa >= 0);
        require(rateDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
        require(slotUnbondDaa >= 0);
        require(slotUnbondDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
    }
    // END oracle bond bounds

    // BEGIN judge bounds
    function checkJudge() {
        require(muBps >= MU_MIN_BPS);
        require(muBps <= MU_MAX_BPS);
        require(roundDaa > 0);
        require(roundDaa <= ROUND_MAX);
        require(ageDaa >= roundDaa);
        require(ageDaa <= AGE_MAX);
        require(unbondDaa >= roundDaa);
        require(unbondDaa <= UNBOND_MAX);
        require(burnBps >= 0);
        require(burnBps <= BURN_MAX_BPS);
        require(minStake >= UNIT);
        require(minStake <= MIN_STAKE_MAX);
    }
    // END judge bounds

    // The oracle market bounds: the same text in KpfOpenO, KpfPairO and KpfPendingO (`oracle_attack_tests`), its
    // pair-parameter lines the same as KpfOpen.checkMarket's where the two families share a parameter. The market id is
    // blake3 of the market body (every parameter and the feed hash), so a block that differs by one byte is another
    // market; every parameter lies in the range that keeps every branch of a pair, a pending part, a slot and a dispute
    // of this market live.
    // BEGIN oracle market bounds
    function checkMarket() {
        require(blake3(ownRs().slice(BODY_AT, BLOCK_END)) == market);
        checkBond();
        checkJudge();
        require(scale > 0);
        require(scale <= SCALE_MAX);
        require(priceMax > 0);
        require(priceMax <= PRICE_CAP);
        require(carrier >= 0);
        require(minSize > 0);
        require(idleDaa >= 0);
        require(idleDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
        require(mmrBps >= 0);
        require(mmrBps < MMR_CAP);
        require(liqFeeBps >= 0);
        require(liqFeeBps <= BPS);
        require(keeperFeeMin >= 0);
        require(bondMin >= 0);
        require(bondMin <= BOND_MIN_MAX);
        require(gBps > 0);
        require(gBps < BPS);
        // A claim is valid only if P + challengeDaa <= X <= P + termDaa + stepDaa, so a window shorter than the term
        // leaves claims possible; 0 < challengeDaa < termDaa < 2^32 (checkBond) is also the CSV range of finalize.
        require(challengeDaa > 0);
        require(challengeDaa < termDaa);
        require(lateDaa >= 0);
        require(lateDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
        require(quietDaa >= 0);
        require(quietDaa < CSV_LIMIT);
        require(sigmaBps >= 0);
        require(sigmaBps <= BPS);
        require(betaBps >= 0);
        require(betaBps <= BPS);
    }
    // END oracle market bounds

    // Contest (docs/DESIGN-ORACLE-2.md 1.7 "Live dispute"): hand the claim to the judge with the opener's stake on NO, as
    // KpfClaimStub.contest. The opener input u is a KpfStake (template JUDGE_TPL, P2SH, canonical state) free stake of
    // this market's judge block, spent by its open entry naming this input as the claim and as the claim's continuation
    // and the dispute at output dOut; the continuation, the dispute and the opener's receipt are exactly the three
    // outputs of this id. KpfStake.open checks the rest (the stake's age before P, the receipt, the dispute's state).
    // The continuation records P (this UTXO's DAA score, refused while unknown) and the opener's key, who receives the
    // disputer's share of the bond if the claim is refuted.
    entry contest(byte[8] ub, byte[8] db) {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        checkMarket();
        require(status == PENDING);
        byte[32] id = OpInputCovenantId(self);
        require(OpCovInputCount(id) == 1);
        require(OpCovOutputCount(id) == 3);
        int p = OpTxInputDaaScore(self);
        require(p >= 0);
        int u = int(ub);
        int d = int(db);
        require(u >= 0);
        require(u < tx.inputs.length);
        require(u != self);
        byte[] st = tplState(u, JUDGE_PRE, STAKE_STATE_LEN, JUDGE_SUF, JUDGE_TPL);
        canon(st);
        require(st.slice(STAKE_STATUS_AT, STAKE_STATUS_AT + 9) == i9(STAKE_FREE));
        require(st.slice(STAKE_MARKET_AT, STAKE_MARKET_END) == judgeBlock(ownRs()));
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigLen(u) == OPEN_HEAD + JUDGE_PRE + STAKE_STATE_LEN + JUDGE_SUF);
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(u, OPEN_TAG_AT, OPEN_HEAD - 3) == byte[](0x04) + byte[](OPEN_TAG));
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(u, OPEN_SIG_AT, OPEN_SIG_AT + 1) == byte[](0x41));
        require(push8(u, 0) == self);
        require(push8(u, 9) == self);
        require(push8(u, 18) == d);
        require(d >= 0);
        require(OpOutputCovenantId(d) == id);
        cont(i9(CONTESTED) + i9(p) + st.slice(0, 33));
    }

    // Decide: the verdict of this part's dispute (input d, resolving onto this input), as KpfClaimStub.decide. Upheld if
    // YES leads, refuted if NO leads; upheld whatever the verdict when the contest was late: this UTXO's own DAA score is
    // the contest's acceptance, and a contest accepted at P + challengeDaa or later came after the window.
    entry decide(byte[8] db) {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        require(status == CONTESTED);
        byte[32] id = OpInputCovenantId(self);
        require(OpCovInputCount(id) == 2);
        require(OpCovOutputCount(id) == 2);
        int d = int(db);
        require(d >= 0);
        require(d < tx.inputs.length);
        require(d != self);
        require(OpInputCovenantId(d) == id);
        byte[] st = tplState(d, JUDGE_PRE, STAKE_STATE_LEN, JUDGE_SUF, JUDGE_TPL);
        require(st.slice(STAKE_STATUS_AT, STAKE_STATUS_AT + 9) == i9(STAKE_DISPUTE));
        byte[] rs = ownRs();
        require(st.slice(STAKE_MARKET_AT, STAKE_MARKET_END) == judgeBlock(rs));
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigLen(d) == RESOLVE_HEAD + JUDGE_PRE + STAKE_STATE_LEN + JUDGE_SUF);
        require(OpTxInputScriptSigSubstr(d, RESOLVE_TAG_AT, RESOLVE_HEAD - 3) == byte[](0x04) + byte[](RESOLVE_TAG));
        require(push8(d, 0) == self);
        int v = REFUTED;
        if (int(byte[8](st.slice(STAKE_SIDE_AT + 1, STAKE_SIDE_AT + 9))) == YES) {
            v = UPHELD;
        }
        int c = OpTxInputDaaScore(self);
        require(c >= 0);
        if (c >= clock + challengeDaa) {
            v = UPHELD;
        }
        cont(i9(v) + rs.slice(STATUS_AT + 9, DISPUTER_END));
    }

    // Cure (DESIGN 4.5d), kind 2 only, while pending. The loser's owner moves its bound exactly to cureBound and repays
    // the proposer (the underwriter) its refund at output i; the cured part holds its range floor and this UTXO's value
    // less the refund plus ceil(q(n, moved distance)), as KpfPending.cure.
    entry cure(sig s) {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        require(OpCovInputCount(OpInputCovenantId(self)) == 1);
        require(status == PENDING);
        require(kind != KIND_CLOSE);
        byte[] z8 = byte[](0 as byte[8]);
        require(cureHash != byte[32](z8 + z8 + z8 + z8));
        int b0 = bl;
        int b1 = bs;
        int add = 0;
        if (side == SIDE_LONG) {
            signedBy(s, longKey);
            b0 = cureBound;
            add = quoteOf(n, bl - cureBound, scale - 1);
        } else {
            signedBy(s, shortKey);
            b1 = cureBound;
            add = quoteOf(n, cureBound - bs, scale - 1);
        }
        only(cureHash, quoteOf(n, b1 - b0, 0) + carrier);
        int o = OpCovOutputIdx(OpInputCovenantId(self), 0);
        require(tx.outputs[o].value - tx.inputs[self].value + refund >= add);
        payTo(self, uwKey, refund);
    }

    // The party the claim could wrong: the other party of a close, the loser of a liquidation.
    function defender() : pubkey {
        pubkey k = longKey;
        if (kind == KIND_CLOSE) {
            if (side == SIDE_LONG) { k = shortKey; }
        } else {
            if (side == SIDE_SHORT) { k = shortKey; }
        }
        return k;
    }

    // A claim that does not settle: the part returns to the restore state with this UTXO's value less the bond; the bond
    // goes to the defender at output i, less the disputer's share floor(B * betaBps / 10^4) at output M - 1 - i (at
    // least the input count) when refuted. A share below dust is not created (the defender gets it); a defender's
    // remainder below dust goes to the disputer.
    function restorePaying(int refuted) {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        only(restoreHash, tx.inputs[self].value - bond);
        int share = 0;
        if (refuted == 1) {
            share = (bond / BPS) * betaBps + ((bond % BPS) * betaBps) / BPS;
        }
        if (share < PLAIN_DUST) { share = 0; }
        int rest = bond - share;
        if (rest < PLAIN_DUST) {
            share = bond;
            rest = 0;
        }
        payTo(self, defender(), rest);
        if (share > 0) {
            int j = tx.outputs.length - 1 - self;
            require(j >= tx.inputs.length);
            payTo(j, disputerKey, share);
        }
    }

    // The settlement of a valid claim (DESIGN 4.5d's finalize with the tolerance g inside the payout). kind 1: the
    // closer is paid at the vouched price moved by g against it (a long at floor(p * (10^4 - g) / 10^4), a short at
    // ceil(p * (10^4 + g) / 10^4), clamped to [bl, bs]) plus its refund at output i (long) or M - 1 - i (short), the other
    // party the rest; no output of the id; a payout of the other party below dust goes to the closer. kind 2 (forfeit and
    // keep): the forfeited part (forfeitHash) with this UTXO's value less B and the fee, the underwriter B + fee at i.
    function settle() {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        byte[32] selfId = OpInputCovenantId(self);
        int v = tx.inputs[self].value;
        if (kind == KIND_CLOSE) {
            require(OpCovOutputCount(selfId) == 0);
            int pc = quote * (BPS - gBps) / BPS;
            if (side == SIDE_SHORT) { pc = (quote * (BPS + gBps) + BPS - 1) / BPS; }
            int c = clampP(pc);
            int owe = quoteOf(n, c - bl, 0);
            if (side == SIDE_SHORT) { owe = quoteOf(n, bs - c, 0); }
            int me = owe + refund;
            int other = v - me;
            if (other < PLAIN_DUST) {
                me = v;
                other = 0;
            }
            int lp = me;
            int sp = other;
            if (side == SIDE_SHORT) {
                lp = other;
                sp = me;
            }
            payTo(self, longKey, lp);
            if (sp > 0) {
                int j = tx.outputs.length - 1 - self;
                require(j >= tx.inputs.length);
                payTo(j, shortKey, sp);
            }
        } else {
            only(forfeitHash, v - bond - fee);
            payTo(self, uwKey, bond + fee);
        }
    }

    // Finalize: anyone. A pending part once challengeDaa old (CSV; its P is its own DAA score), an upheld or refuted
    // part at once (its P is the recorded one). Refuted: restore, the bond to the defender and the disputer. Otherwise
    // the claim settles if it is valid and is restored with the bond to the defender if it is void.
    entry finalize() {
        int self = this.activeInputIndex;
        require(OpCovInputCount(OpInputCovenantId(self)) == 1);
        int p = clock;
        if (status == PENDING) {
            require(this.ageDaa >= challengeDaa);
            p = OpTxInputDaaScore(self);
            require(p >= 0);
        } else {
            require(status == UPHELD || status == REFUTED);
        }
        if (status == REFUTED) {
            restorePaying(1);
        } else {
            int valid = 1;
            if (p + challengeDaa > expiry) { valid = 0; }
            if (expiry > p + termDaa + stepDaa) { valid = 0; }
            if (p - t0 > lateDaa) { valid = 0; }
            if (valid == 1) {
                settle();
            } else {
                restorePaying(0);
            }
        }
    }
}
